Thus plan:

- Activate origin node
- Load origin payload (occupied, lock)
- Unload origin payload (makes ready true, confirmed true, cargo available)
Now origin_node_occupied true (still), origin_node_ready true (from unload), origin_availability_locked true (still), origin_availability_confirmed true (from unload). That's fine.

Now cargo_available true again.

- Activate destination node
- Load destination payload (occupied, lock)
- Unload destination payload (makes ready true, confirmed true, cargo available)

Now we have both nodes occupied and ready, both availabilities locked and confirmed (origin also confirmed). Goal only requires destination confirmed and locked, not origin; but origin confirmed true is okay.

Now we need to ensure candidate_prepared for destination before activation etc. So we need to do attach_task_profile, allocate vehicle, confirm candidate preparedness, assign operator, then activate, load, unload.

Now we also need to ensure transport leg assembly and loading authorized etc.

